// =============================================================================
// stdlib.lumen — the standard-library pack (generalised annotation resources)
// =============================================================================
// A RECORD of what the stdlib owes the other packs, landed with #403 so the issue
// pack's `computed labels` / `comments` projections have a type to resolve against.
// This is the as-needed shape, NOT the finished generalisation: the real
// define + implement + prove pass runs in parallel (a background effort), and the
// two reconcile in a later sweep — see the OPEN sidebar in §1.
//
// SCOPE — what lives here:
//   Annotation — a rev-neutral resource that points AT a target resource and
//   carries its own payload. Label and Comment are the two concrete annotations
//   the issue pack leans on today; both generalise a per-target annotation from a
//   single target type to any resource.
//
// PRINCIPLES:
//   1. Annotations are rev-neutral. Creating, editing or deleting an annotation
//      never advances its target's revision, emits no change event on the target,
//      and never enters the target's content hash. The annotation carries its own
//      identity, revision history and provenance; its OWN revision advances normally.
//   2. Point AT, don't own. An annotation is a first-class resource that names its
//      target by ref — it is NOT a field on the target. The target's view of its
//      annotations (issue.lumen `labels` / `comments`) is a COMPUTED projection.
//   3. Record now, generalise later. These shapes capture what the model needs
//      today; the rel<>-vs-resource question (§1 OPEN) is deferred to the sweep.
// =============================================================================

/// description: Free text — a nominal string.
type text is string


// #############################################################################
// §1. The model
// #############################################################################

// > **Open** — whether an Annotation is better carried as a `rel<resource, …>`
// > edge (like issue.lumen's Dependency) rather than a resource with a `target`
// > property, and whether the issue pack keeps `labels` / `comments` as computed
// > projections over this model or folds them in, is the generalisation question.
// > Deferred to the reconciliation sweep; the parallel define + implement + prove
// > effort owns it.

/// description: Annotation — a rev-neutral resource that points AT a target resource and carries its own payload. `abstract` — only the concrete annotations below are instantiated.
/// normative: Rev-neutral — writing or removing an Annotation NEVER advances its `target`'s revision, emits no change event on the target, and never enters the target's content hash. The Annotation has its own identity, revision history and provenance; its own revision advances normally.
/// normative: An Annotation names its `target` by ref and is NOT a field on the target. A target's view of its annotations is a COMPUTED projection (see issue.lumen `labels` / `comments`).
abstract type Annotation is Resource {
  target: ref<resource>,          // the annotated resource
}

/// description: Comment — free-text commentary on a target resource.
/// normative: `author` is a native human/agent string — NOT a BDP attribution ref. `body` is the comment text.
type Comment is Annotation {
  body:    text,
  author?: text,                  // native author string — NOT a ref
}

/// description: Label — a named tag on a target resource.
/// normative: The natural key is (`target`, `name`) — at most one Label of a given `name` on a given target. Whether this is spelled `unique` (as on a rel) or as a resource natural-key constraint is settled in the sweep.
type Label is Annotation {
  name: text,
}
